 "open_points": [
  "Market: the paper (letters-and-print.json issue_02) prints the Copper Row market on Tuesday, Friday and Saturday; the ruled calendar (2.1.6) and G9 say Thursday. Thursday wins; fix the paper line. The map has no market square: the ruled market stays in Copper Row (off the map) and a small row of pitches is chosen for the quay road's north pavement (places.json market_stalls_quay).",
  "Bonfire Night: the blueprint says a display on the quay, adults only; the brief wants a bonfire on waste ground. Both are built on Monday 5 Nov: bonfire 18:30 to 22:00 on the waste ground behind Basin Top (chosen, free ground), display 19:30 to 20:00 on the quay.",
  "Remembrance Sunday: 11 Nov 1990 is a Sunday (checked). Kept at the chapel, service 10:30, silence 11:00 (times chosen).",
  "Christmas lies outside the seven-week calendar (it ends Sun 2 Dec); Christmas Day, Tuesday 25 Dec 1990, applies only once the clock has run on after the ending. Its rules are chosen.",
  "Match Saturdays follow the paper's results: home 27 Oct, 10 Nov, 1 Dec; away 20 Oct, 3 Nov, 17 Nov and (chosen) 24 Nov. The paper has Northwold Rangers at Ropewalk Park on both 10 Nov and 1 Dec, and Easterby United at home on 13 Oct; the 24 Nov ground is not stated. G9's doubling 'at 15:00 and 17:00 for half an hour' is read as the half hours before kick-off and after the final whistle (chosen). The paper should state 24 Nov's ground.",
  "Cold-store shift: the brief's 17:30 and the blueprint's half past five mornings are both kept (day shift leaves 17:30; night shift leaves 05:30). Which one is the 'packing shift' fare of 3.x needs the keeper's word; the contract test (2.15.2) uses the morning shift.",
  "Drivers: BLUEPRINT-02 2.7 says a £90 weekly wage per driver; the 24 Nov economy choice is half of each car's takings (about £65 to £125 a week). The economy wins; the wages_dock_cold row is for dockers and cold-store hands only. The Friday reckoning at the counter is chosen.",
  "Rent: £18 every Friday to Mr Leonard Askew of Agar & Co's agents at Mickey's counter, time 11:00 to 12:00 chosen. The story frame's Dawn Pybus (running for the rent collector) is not used (letters-and-print.json open point).",
  "Early closing: none built (see shop_hours.early_closing_note); shop-hours-1990 found Thursday as Hull's early-closing day but no 1990 source.",
  "Beat: G5's cycle of about 7 real minutes is real time, so at 2 s a game minute a 22:00 to 06:00 night holds about 2.4 cycles (about 200 game minutes each). The doors-in-sight standards of G5 still hold (4 and 7.5 real minutes).",
  "Ferry: half-hourly until 17:30 and the last crossing from the Hook at 23:00 Monday to Saturday are the paper's; the minutes (:10 and :40 arrivals, away five minutes later) and the Sunday service are chosen. Tom's 15:40 arrival on Monday 15 Oct is a regular :40 arrival.",
  "Bin day (Wednesday), post, paper-delivery and bus times, milk float's route, the second post: chosen (no source). Milk float 05:30 to 07:30 is sounds.json's.",
  "Dated paper events are fixed in print (the paper's dates do not move with story state): the jumble sale, meetings, gas main, berths, the dance. Items marked story_check (customs seizure 31 Oct, licensing 15 Nov, dock gate chaining 1 Dec) print only if their state holds.",
  "Clock recomputations are in real_time (old figures at 60 s a game hour, new at 120 s)."
 ],
